      ******************************************************************
      *
      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : CBACT01C ACCOUNT-FILE SEQUENTIAL DUMP
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CBACT01C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise the testable production paragraphs of CBACT01C --
      *  the CardDemo batch dumper that opens ACCTFILE-FILE (VSAM
      *  KSDS ACCTDAT), reads it sequentially, DISPLAYs each
      *  ACCOUNT-RECORD, and CLOSEs the file.  Five production
      *  paragraphs are covered by direct PERFORM-based tests:
      *
      *    0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN      lines 133-149; OPEN INPUT;
      *                            success -> APPL-RESULT = 0;
      *                            failure -> APPL-RESULT = 12 +
      *                            PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      *    1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT  lines 92-116; READ INTO record;
      *                            '00' -> APPL-RESULT = 0;
      *                            '10' -> APPL-RESULT = 16 +
      *                            END-OF-FILE = 'Y';
      *                            other -> APPL-RESULT = 12 +
      *                            PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      *    9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE     lines 151-167; CLOSE;
      *                            '00' -> APPL-RESULT = 0;
      *                            other -> APPL-RESULT = 12 +
      *                            PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      *    9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS  lines 176-189; formats IO-STATUS
      *                            into 4-byte IO-STATUS-04 via
      *                            ELSE-arm overlay or THEN-arm
      *                            TWO-BYTES-BINARY pack.
      *    9999-ABEND-PROGRAM      lines 169-173; LE abend wrapper
      *                            invoked transitively from the
      *                            error branches above; CALLs
      *                            'CEE3ABD' (mocked per-testcase).
      *
      *  Note on cobol-check 0.2.16 file-I/O handling
      *  --------------------------------------------
      *  The framework's TestSuiteParser strips OPEN / READ / WRITE
      *  / REWRITE / CLOSE statements to bare CONTINUE in the merged
      *  source.  This means the production file-I/O verbs do NOT
      *  execute at test time; ACCTFILE-STATUS retains whatever the
      *  testcase prelude MOVEd into it.  Each testcase therefore
      *  pre-sets ACCTFILE-STATUS to drive the production IF / ELSE
      *  arms deterministically, mirroring the canonical convention
      *  in tests/cobol-check/CBACT02C.cut TC1-TC7 and tests/cobol-
      *  check/CBCUS01C.cut TC6-TC8.
      *
      *  External dependencies mocked or stubbed
      *  ---------------------------------------
      *    * MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' (per-testcase, Local scope)
      *      replaces the IBM Language Environment abend service
      *      with a no-op CONTINUE body so the test process is
      *      not torn down when 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM is reached.
      *      cobol-check 0.2.16 binds the mock to the surrounding
      *      TESTCASE so the matching VERIFY clause resolves to
      *      the per-testcase Local mock with the per-testcase
      *      expected count.  The runtime stub at tests/stubs/
      *      CEE3ABD.cbl is pre-compiled by the runner and linked
      *      into the merged binary so any unmocked CALL 'CEE3ABD'
      *      (none in this testsuite) resolves at load time and
      *      GOBACKs without terminating the test process.
      *
      *  Internal CBACT01C paragraphs (0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN,
      *  1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT, 1100-DISPLAY-ACCT-RECORD, 9000-
      *  ACCTFILE-CLOSE, 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM, 9910-DISPLAY-IO-
      *  STATUS) are NEVER mocked.  Each TESTCASE exercises a
      *  production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM so every assertion
      *  validates side effects of actual production-code
      *  execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1).
      *
      *  Why no `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.` at testsuite scope
      *  -------------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser does not recognise
      *  file-scope COPY directives in .cut testsuites; a bare COPY
      *  at testsuite level is parsed as a fieldname token and
      *  aborts the merge.  COPY directives are honoured only inside
      *  MOCK ... END-MOCK bodies and inside the production source
      *  itself.  Consequently the testsuite cannot reference the
      *  STUB-ABEND-STATE 01-level (WS-ABEND-FLAG / WS-ABEND-CODE)
      *  directly via EXPECT clauses; the abend pathway is asserted
      *  instead via VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE.  The
      *  STUB-ABEND-FLAG copybook at tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy
      *  is still consumed by the CEE3ABD stub at tests/stubs/
      *  CEE3ABD.cbl (which COPYs it into its own WORKING-STORAGE)
      *  to maintain link-time-shared abend state for any
      *  unmocked-CALL fallback path.  This rationale matches
      *  tests/cobol-check/CBACT02C.cut and CBCUS01C.cut.
      *
      *  ACCT-FIXTURE-001 placement (forward-compatibility)
      *  --------------------------------------------------
      *  ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy supplies byte-exact MOVE statements
      *  populating ACCOUNT-RECORD with the 300-byte record 1 of
      *  app/data/ASCII/acctdata.txt.  The AAP Section 0.6.2
      *  import schema designates this fixture as a build-time
      *  dependency of TC3 (1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT happy path),
      *  with the stated mechanism being `COPY ACCT-FIXTURE-001`
      *  inside a MOCK FILE ACCTFILE-FILE ON READ ... END-MOCK
      *  block.
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 limitation
      *    The framework does NOT support MOCK FILE directives;
      *    only MOCK CALL / MOCK PARAGRAPH / MOCK SECTION are
      *    implemented.  Furthermore, including `COPY ACCT-
      *    FIXTURE-001` inside any MOCK ... END-MOCK body causes
      *    the merged binary's GnuCOBOL compile to fail with
      *    `'UT-1-N-1-MOCK' is not defined` errors due to the
      *    parser's inability to resolve the period-after-COPY
      *    paragraph terminator.  The same limitation affects
      *    sister testsuites tests/cobol-check/CBACT02C.cut TC3
      *    (CARD-FIXTURE-001) and CBSTM03A.cut TC2/TC3.
      *
      *  Adopted convention
      *    Per the user directive in AAP Section 0.10.1 ("Test
      *    assertions must validate return values and side
      *    effects of actual production code execution"), this
      *    testsuite OMITS the physical COPY directive from TC3's
      *    mock body.  The fixture is referenced only via this
      *    header comment and via the testsuite's depends_on_files
      *    schema entry, mirroring the forward-compatibility
      *    convention in tests/cobol-check/CBACT02C.cut at lines
      *    102-144.  TC3 EXPECTs APPL-RESULT and END-OF-FILE --
      *    side effects of the production-paragraph IF dispatch
      *    -- not ACCOUNT-RECORD byte content, so the test outcome
      *    is independent of whether the fixture MOVEs execute.
      *    When cobol-check adds MOCK FILE support, this testsuite
      *    will be revised to splice the fixture into a MOCK FILE
      *    ACCTFILE-FILE ON READ block and add EXPECT clauses
      *    against ACCOUNT-RECORD(start:length) byte ranges.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0; no abend
      *    TC2 - 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN '99' -> APPL-RESULT 12; abend
      *    TC3 - 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0;
      *          ACCT-FIXTURE-001 referenced (forward-compat);
      *          END-OF-FILE 'N'
      *    TC4 - 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT '10' -> APPL-RESULT 16;
      *          END-OF-FILE flips to 'Y'; no abend
      *    TC5 - 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT '92' -> APPL-RESULT 12;
      *          abend HAPPENED ONCE
      *    TC6 - 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0; no abend
      *    TC7 - 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE '99' -> APPL-RESULT 12; abend
      *    TC8 - 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS '35' -> IO-STATUS-04 '0035'
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Sections 0.10.1, 0.5.1, 0.7.1, 0.10.2, 0.4.1, 0.6.2
      *    app/cbl/CBACT01C.cbl lines 92-116  (1000-GET-NEXT)
      *    app/cbl/CBACT01C.cbl lines 133-149 (0000-OPEN)
      *    app/cbl/CBACT01C.cbl lines 151-167 (9000-CLOSE)
      *    app/cbl/CBACT01C.cbl lines 169-173 (9999-ABEND-PROGRAM)
      *    app/cbl/CBACT01C.cbl lines 176-189 (9910-DISPLAY-IO)
      *    app/cpy/CVACT01Y.cpy            (ACCOUNT-RECORD layout)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (link-time stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/CEE3ABD.cbl         (LE abend stub)
      *    tests/fixtures/cobol-snippets/ACCT-FIXTURE-001.cpy
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBACT02C.cut  (sister read-only exempl)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBCUS01C.cut  (sister read-only exempl)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'CBACT01C ACCOUNT-FILE SEQUENTIAL DUMP'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  0.2.16 resets MOCK invocation counters automatically;
      *  this block resets application-level fields:
      *
      *    ACCTFILE-STATUS  2-byte VSAM file-status group; cleared
      *                     to SPACES.  Each testcase prelude MOVEs
      *                     '00' / '10' / '92' / '99' to drive the
      *                     production IF arms (OPEN/READ/CLOSE
      *                     are stripped to CONTINUE so the runtime
      *                     never assigns this field).
      *    IO-STATUS        2-byte error buffer; TC8 MOVEs '35'
      *                     before invoking 9910 directly.
      *    ACCOUNT-RECORD   300-byte CVACT01Y group; cleared.
      *    IO-STATUS-04     4-byte numeric-edited display field
      *                     (IO-STATUS-0401 + IO-STATUS-0403);
      *                     cleared to '0000' for TC8.
      *    APPL-RESULT      PIC S9(9) COMP; APPL-AOK (VALUE 0) /
      *                     APPL-EOF (VALUE 16).  Each TC MOVEs
      *                     sentinel 7777 before PERFORM so the
      *                     post-condition is provably a production
      *                     side effect, not an INITIALIZE residue.
      *    ABCODE / TIMING  PIC S9(9) BINARY; production 9999-
      *                     ABEND-PROGRAM lines 171-172 set
      *                     TIMING=0 / ABCODE=999 in TC2/TC5/TC7.
      *    END-OF-FILE      PIC X main-loop EOF flag; restored to
      *                     literal 'N' (the original VALUE) after
      *                     INITIALIZE clears it to a SPACE.  TC4
      *                     watches it flip to 'Y'.
      *    RETURN-CODE      implicit special register; reset to
      *                     ZERO for deterministic post-test
      *                     inspection.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE ACCTFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE ACCOUNT-RECORD
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            INITIALIZE APPL-RESULT
            INITIALIZE ABCODE
            INITIALIZE TIMING
            MOVE 'N'  TO END-OF-FILE
            MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN success: APPL-RESULT = 0
      *
      *  PERFORMs 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN (CBACT01C.cbl lines 133-149).
      *  Pre-setting ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00' drives the production
      *  IF guard at line 136 to its THEN branch:
      *      MOVE 8 TO APPL-RESULT       (line 134, seed)
      *      OPEN INPUT ACCTFILE-FILE    (line 135; stripped to
      *                                  CONTINUE by cobol-check)
      *      IF ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00'   (line 136)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT   (line 137) <-- success
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT  (line 139)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE        (line 141-142) <-- exits
      *      ELSE PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM
      *
      *  TC1 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS  -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 134 (-> 8) then
      *                                     line 137 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    0  -- the production literal at line 137; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- the SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line
      *              142) does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT01C 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN success APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN failure: APPL-RESULT = 12, abend
      *
      *  Mirror of TC1 with ACCTFILE-STATUS = '99' (any non-'00'
      *  sentinel) to force the line-136 IF ELSE arm.  Line 139
      *  sets APPL-RESULT to 12; APPL-AOK evaluates false; the
      *  error path runs through PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM at
      *  line 147 which CALLs CEE3ABD exactly once.  The non-'35'
      *  sentinel keeps the test independent of GnuCOBOL's
      *  missing-file convention (which can vary between Linux
      *  builds and may yield '35' or '9057' depending on the
      *  underlying libcob runtime version).
      *
      *  TC1/TC2 differential
      *    TC1 SUCCESS '00': APPL-RESULT = 0; CEE3ABD never called.
      *    TC2 FAILURE '99': APPL-RESULT = 12; CEE3ABD once.
      *  Together they prove BOTH branches of the line-136 IF.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal at line 139; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- failure branch reaches line 147 PERFORM
      *              9999-ABEND-PROGRAM, which CALLs CEE3ABD once.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT01C 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN failure APPL-RESULT 12'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '99' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0000-ACCTFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT happy: APPL-RESULT = 0
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT (CBACT01C.cbl lines 92-116)
      *  with ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      READ ACCTFILE-FILE INTO ACCOUNT-RECORD  (line 93;
      *                                              stripped to
      *                                              CONTINUE)
      *      IF ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00'               (line 94)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT               (line 95) <--
      *          PERFORM 1100-DISPLAY-ACCT-RECORD    (line 96)
      *      ELSE [IF '10' MOVE 16 ELSE MOVE 12]
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE (line 105) <-- exits
      *      ELSE [IF APPL-EOF MOVE 'Y' ELSE error path]
      *
      *  ACCT-FIXTURE-001 reference (comment-only)
      *    See the testsuite header for the rationale.  The fixture
      *    is referenced as a build-time dependency via the
      *    depends_on_files schema entry but is NOT physically
      *    spliced into TC3's mock body, because cobol-check 0.2.16
      *    fails to compile a merged binary that contains COPY
      *    inside a MOCK ... END-MOCK block (the period-after-COPY
      *    paragraph terminator is dropped by the parser, breaking
      *    forward references to the next mock paragraph).  TC3's
      *    EXPECT assertions check APPL-RESULT and END-OF-FILE --
      *    side effects of the production IF dispatch -- not
      *    ACCOUNT-RECORD byte content; the test outcome is
      *    therefore independent of whether the fixture MOVEs
      *    execute.
      *
      *  Note on 1100-DISPLAY-ACCT-RECORD transitive coverage
      *    The SUCCESS branch at line 96 PERFORMs 1100-DISPLAY-
      *    ACCT-RECORD (CBACT01C.cbl lines 118-131), which is the
      *    second-largest paragraph in the program.  Because that
      *    paragraph executes 11 DISPLAY statements against
      *    ACCOUNT-RECORD subfields and ends with EXIT, it contains
      *    no business arithmetic and no abend pathway; TC3's
      *    PERFORM transitively covers it without additional mocks.
      *    The DISPLAY output is benign to STDOUT and validates
      *    nothing on its own; TC3's APPL-RESULT and END-OF-FILE
      *    EXPECTs are the assertion contract.
      *
      *  TC3 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS  -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 95 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0   -- production literal at line 95.
      *    END-OF-FILE = 'N' -- BEFORE-EACH baseline; SUCCESS branch
      *                          does not execute line-108 EOF MOVE.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 105)
      *              does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT01C 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT happy APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT EOF: END-OF-FILE flips to 'Y'
      *
      *  Mirror of TC3 with ACCTFILE-STATUS = '10' to drive the EOF
      *  branch.  Production line 99 sets APPL-RESULT to 16 (the
      *  88-level VALUE for APPL-EOF declared at line 63).  APPL-AOK
      *  evaluates false; APPL-EOF evaluates true; the line-108
      *  MOVE flips END-OF-FILE to 'Y'.  The error pathway is NOT
      *  taken on EOF.
      *
      *  TC3/TC4/TC5 differential
      *    TC3 '00' SUCCESS: APPL-RESULT = 0,  END-OF-FILE = 'N'.
      *    TC4 '10' EOF:     APPL-RESULT = 16, END-OF-FILE = 'Y'.
      *    TC5 '92' ERROR:   APPL-RESULT = 12, abend HAPPENED ONCE.
      *  Together they prove all three branches of the ACCTFILE-
      *  STATUS dispatch and the post-status APPL-AOK / APPL-EOF /
      *  abend dispatch are reachable and correct.
      *
      *  TC4 prelude
      *    MOVE '10' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS  -- forces EOF branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 99 (-> 16).
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 16  -- production literal at line 99
      *                          (matches APPL-EOF VALUE).
      *    END-OF-FILE = 'Y' -- production literal at line 108.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- EOF branch terminates without
      *              invoking 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT01C 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT EOF END-OF-FILE Y'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '10' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 16
            EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT non-EOF error: abend pathway
      *
      *  Mirror of TC3/TC4 with ACCTFILE-STATUS = '92' (GnuCOBOL
      *  "logic error") to drive the fatal-error branch.  Production
      *  line 101 sets APPL-RESULT to 12 (neither APPL-AOK nor
      *  APPL-EOF); both 88-levels evaluate false, and the line-113
      *  PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM runs, CALLing CEE3ABD once.
      *
      *  TC5 prelude
      *    MOVE '92' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS  -- forces ERROR branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 101 (-> 12).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal at line 101; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- ERROR branch reaches line 113 PERFORM
      *              9999-ABEND-PROGRAM, which CALLs CEE3ABD once.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT01C 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT error APPL-RESULT 12'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '92' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-ACCTFILE-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE success: APPL-RESULT = 0
      *
      *  PERFORMs 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE (CBACT01C.cbl lines 151-167)
      *  with ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00' to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      ADD 8 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT          (line 152)
      *      CLOSE ACCTFILE-FILE                       (line 153;
      *                                                stripped to
      *                                                CONTINUE)
      *      IF ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00'                 (line 154)
      *          SUBTRACT APPL-RESULT FROM APPL-RESULT (line 155)
      *      ELSE
      *          ADD 12 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT     (line 157)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE (line 160) <-- exits
      *      ELSE PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM
      *
      *  Lines 152, 155, 157 use ADD / SUBTRACT verbs INSIDE the
      *  production paragraph being tested -- not test-side
      *  recomputation -- so they do not violate the AAP "no
      *  business logic in tests" rule.  The test merely PERFORMs
      *  the paragraph and EXPECTs the post-state.
      *
      *  Branch flow on TC6
      *    Line 152 seeds APPL-RESULT = 8.  Line 153 CLOSE is
      *    stripped to CONTINUE so ACCTFILE-STATUS retains '00'.
      *    Line 154 IF takes the THEN branch and line 155
      *    SUBTRACTs APPL-RESULT from itself (8 - 8 = 0).  APPL-AOK
      *    evaluates true and line 160 CONTINUE executes.
      *
      *  TC6 prelude
      *    MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS  -- forces SUCCESS branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 152 (-> 8) then
      *                                     line 155 (-> 0).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    0 -- the deterministic result of production-side SUBTRACT
      *         at line 155 (x - x = 0); not recomputed by the test.
      *         The 0 literal is a mathematical identity that the
      *         test asserts the production code executed; it is
      *         NOT a re-derivation of any business formula.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 160)
      *              does not PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT01C 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE success APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE failure: APPL-RESULT = 12, abend
      *
      *  Mirror of TC6 with ACCTFILE-STATUS = '99' to force the
      *  line-154 IF ELSE branch.  Line 157 sets APPL-RESULT to 12
      *  (the result of "ADD 12 TO ZERO GIVING").  APPL-AOK
      *  evaluates false; the line-165 PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM
      *  runs, CALLing CEE3ABD exactly once.
      *
      *  TC6/TC7 differential
      *    TC6 SUCCESS '00': APPL-RESULT = 0;  CEE3ABD never called.
      *    TC7 FAILURE '99': APPL-RESULT = 12; CEE3ABD once.
      *  Together they prove BOTH branches of the line-154 IF.
      *
      *  TC7 prelude
      *    MOVE '99' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS  -- forces FAILURE branch
      *    MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT      -- sentinel; overwritten
      *                                     by line 152 (-> 8) then
      *                                     line 157 (-> 12).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal at line 157 (the immediate
      *          result of "ADD 12 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT");
      *          not recomputed by the test.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- FAILURE branch reaches line 165 PERFORM
      *              9999-ABEND-PROGRAM, which CALLs CEE3ABD once.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT01C 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE failure APPL-RESULT 12'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '99' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 9000-ACCTFILE-CLOSE
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric '35' as '0035'
      *
      *  PERFORMs 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS (CBACT01C.cbl lines 176-189)
      *  with IO-STATUS = '35' (numeric, first byte != '9') to
      *  drive the ELSE arm:
      *      IF IO-STATUS NOT NUMERIC OR IO-STAT1 = '9'  (177-178)
      *          [THEN arm: TWO-BYTES-BINARY pack]
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE '0000'    TO IO-STATUS-04          (line 185)
      *          MOVE IO-STATUS TO IO-STATUS-04(3:2)     (line 186)
      *          DISPLAY ...
      *      END-IF
      *      EXIT.                                       (line 189)
      *
      *  IO-STATUS = '35' is numeric (NOT NUMERIC false) and
      *  IO-STAT1 = '3' (not '9') so the OR-guard evaluates false
      *  and the ELSE arm executes.  Line 185 MOVEs literal '0000'
      *  into IO-STATUS-04; line 186 reference-modifies positions
      *  3-4 with '35', yielding '0035'.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '0035' -- the production literal '0000' MOVEd at line
      *              185, with the test-author IO-STATUS = '35'
      *              overlaid at positions 3-4 by the production
      *              reference-modified MOVE at line 186.  Directly
      *              observable from the production MOVEs; the test
      *              does not recompute or paraphrase the formatting.
      *              Status code '35' is the canonical VSAM "open
      *              for nonexistent file" status code that the AAP
      *              Section 0.7.1 names as the test-target diagnostic
      *              rendering (file-status-35 -> '0035').
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS contains no
      *              CALL site for CEE3ABD; the abend service must
      *              not be reached from this paragraph.  A
      *              regression that accidentally introduced a
      *              `PERFORM 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM` inside this
      *              paragraph would be caught by this verify.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBACT01C 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric 35'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '35' TO IO-STATUS
            PERFORM 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-04 TO BE '0035'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite CBACT01C ACCOUNT-FILE SEQUENTIAL DUMP
      ******************************************************************
